/-!
Slice S5 of the Erdős #1041 formalisation: the two explicit paths inside `Ω(f)` of §4.2,
delivered as `Erdos1041.Counterexample.s5_roots_connected_to_critical`.

The 109 supplied subdivisions of the two rational-centre polylines are replaced by four
whole-segment degree-fourteen Bernstein certificates with positive integer coefficients
(`P3a`, `P3b`, `P6a`, `P6b`).  On top of that the file carries the three endpoint joins:

* `joined_zs_wq` — the straight segment from the interior critical point to the rational
  centre `wq`, inside the certified positive disc of radius `10⁻⁸`.  The `10⁻⁸`
  localisation is obtained from the coarse `ρε/1000` localisation by an exact Taylor
  sharpening of `Q'` about `wq` (`delta_small`);
* `endpoint3` / `endpoint6` — the positive-sector bridge from the rational endpoints
  `m₃`, `m₆` to `8ζⱼ`, followed by the physical radial segment down to the roots.

The localisation of the interior critical point is read off slice S4's `s4_instance_critical`.
-/

